<title>POLAND: Warsaw bourse confirms KGHM July 10 listing.</title>
<headline>Warsaw bourse confirms KGHM July 10 listing.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Warsaw Stock Exchange set the first listing of Poland's KGHM Polska Miedz SA copper concern for July 10, the date earlier announced by the company.</p>
<p>&quot;The first listing of KGHM Polska Miedz SA will take place on July 10,&quot; a deputy president of the bourse, Ryszard Czerniawski, told a news conference.</p>
<p>The bourse approved for trading 150 million out of 200 million KGHM's shares.</p>
<p>The state treasury earmarked 30 million shares to be offered to KGHM employees for free and 20 million shares for pension funds to be set up under Poland's social security reform and these shares will not be available for the bourse trade.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
